    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a source of deep fascination for me. As someone who values logic and structure, I see math as a language that helps us understand patterns in the world. I enjoy solving problems and exploring abstract ideas, especially in areas like algebra and philosophy of math. It’s both challenging and deeply rewarding, much like studying human nature.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "I do feel some anxiety when faced with complex or unfamiliar math problems, especially under time pressure. But I’ve learned to manage it through mindfulness and breaking problems into smaller steps. My high neuroticism makes me more sensitive to stress, but my openness helps me approach challenges with curiosity rather than fear. I remind myself that mistakes are part of learning.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used an AI tutor app to review calculus concepts. It provided step-by-step explanations and practice problems tailored to my level. The interface was intuitive, and I appreciated how it offered multiple approaches to solving problems. It helped me build confidence, though I still needed to verify results manually. It’s a useful tool, not a replacement for deep understanding.",
